This study introduces the task of symptom event extraction designed to deliver generalizable capabilities across diverse clinical domains. We present SymBERT, a method that achieves state-ofthe-art performance by integrating multiple data augmentation strategies, leveraging pre-trained models, and applying self-supervised learning. We also establish two novel multiclass clinical datasets drawn from Epic's Blue Star Data Platform, which feature distinct distributions to thoroughly assess model robustness. Furthermore, we compiled a specialized annotation guideline to address inherent ambiguities when labeling symptoms. We release our source code and the annotated data via a dedicated repository at https://github.com/CMU-SOM-ai-lab/steme, which is also accessible at https://github.com/CMU-SOM-ai-lab/steme.

